  "claim": "The company that Italian-born Chick Lang, Sr. was general manager of, operates a race track in the largest municipality in the Maryland county Prince George's County.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Maryland Jockey Club. Sentence: After 267 years it remains the corporate name of the company that operates; Pimlico Race Course in Baltimore, Maryland which opened in 1870, Laurel Park Racecourse in Laurel, Maryland which opened in 1911 and Bowie Race Track in Bowie, Maryland which opened as race course in 1914 and ceased operations as a track in 1985.\nPage: Bowie, Maryland. Sentence: Bowie has grown from a small railroad stop to the largest municipality in Prince George's County, and the fifth most populous city and third largest city by area in the U.S. state of Maryland.\nPage: Chick Lang, Sr.. Sentence: Charles John \"Chick\" Lang, Sr. (1926 – March 18, 2010) was an American businessman and general manager of the Maryland Jockey Club.",
