        "original_id": "3b6f74c5-8c2e-5cb2-bb73-684279dcb874",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Maryland Jockey Club\n- Places: Pimlico Race Course, Laurel Park Racecourse, Bowie Race Track, Bowie, Baltimore, Laurel, Prince George's County, Maryland\n- People: Charles John \"Chick\" Lang, Sr.\n- Roles: general manager, businessman\n\nFacts:\n- The Maryland Jockey Club has remained the corporate name of the company that operates Pimlico Race Course, Laurel Park Racecourse, and Bowie Race Track for 267 years.\n- Pimlico Race Course in Baltimore, Maryland, opened in 1870.\n- Laurel Park Racecourse in Laurel, Maryland, opened in 1911.\n- Bowie Race Track in Bowie, Maryland, opened as a race course in 1914.\n- Bowie Race Track ceased operating as a track in 1985.\n- Charles John \"Chick\" Lang, Sr. was born in 1926.\n- Bowie grew from a small railroad stop into the largest municipality in Prince George's County, the fifth most populous city in Maryland, and the third largest Maryland city by area.\n- Charles John \"Chick\" Lang, Sr. was an American businessman and the general manager of the Maryland Jockey Club.\n- Charles John \"Chick\" Lang, Sr. died on March 18, 2010.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
